      "message": "This is getting a bit complicated for my taste.  If I was doing this I think I would keep the parameters to GPIO well defined and change the second and third parameters to a single one called pin.  Then have that parameters meaning be architecture dependent.  MEC would:\n\n#define GPIO_PIN(number) (number / 10), (1 \u003c\u003c (gpionum%10))\n\nand STM32 would:\n\n#define GPIO_PIN(port, pin) port, pin\n\nI would also do something similar with the SHORTNAMES define, I would change that to a function macro that takes name, port, and pin, and constructs a GPIO name from that, then each board can define that at will.  The result would be no convoluted #if logic in this file, which would be better.",
